  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive sample of half life <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>23</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>days</mi></math>&nbsp;is disintegrating continuously. The percentage decay of&nbsp;the sample&nbsp;between the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>15</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>16</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math> day&nbsp;will be [Take, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></math>]"
